Also inspired by arcade games, we designed the visual style around an old television screen. Since we did not have enough time to create animations, our artist designed a small robot that moved around on wheels instead.&#x20;

Our narrative designer also wrote several short pieces of backstory for the game, which were recorded as news broadcasts and played at the beginning of the game and at the end of each round. We also created a simple TV power-on and power-off effect to transition between the screen-on and screen-off phases.

As a result, despite the extremely limited development time, we still managed to create a relatively complete game. This was probably the aspect of the project that I was most satisfied with.
